A community garden at dawn. Rows of beans and a crooked scarecrow.

EXT. COMMUNITY GARDEN - DAWN

A TALL STRANGER (50s), lanky, close-cropped grey hair, denim jacket, paint-stained hands, kneels by the water barrel. Patient and quiet.

MARA waters the tomatoes and watches him over her shoulder.

TALL STRANGER
Your beans need staking before noon.

MARA
I know. Tall Stranger fixed the shed roof.

TALL STRANGER
Nobody sent me. I'm just here to help.

INT. GARDEN SHED - MORNING

TALL STRANGER sorts seed packets on a crate, one at a time.

MARA
You knew where the trowels were.

TALL STRANGER
I used to garden here.

EXT. GARDEN GATE - EVENING

TALL STRANGER leans on the gate. A bicycle bell rings somewhere down the lane.

NED
Is he staying for supper?

TALL STRANGER
Tell my sister the ladder is back.

MARA
Tell her yourself.

TALL STRANGER
I will, when the beans are staked.
